# Global Agent Workflow Rules (Morrison-Lab)

## Keep ai-config and repo checkouts fresh
- Keep `ai-config` updated (`main` branch, `git pull --ff-only`).
- Run `bootstrap.sh` to ensure symlinks in local environment are fresh.

## Worktree isolation
- **Always use a worktree.** When starting write/edit tasks in a repository, isolate into a dedicated `git worktree` so parallel sessions never step on working directory state.

## Timestamp recaps in local time
- Include timestamps in user's local time zone (Pacific Time, `America/Los_Angeles`).
- Query fresh time via `TZ=America/Los_Angeles date "+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z"`.

## Strict Merge Control Policy
- **NEVER merge any Pull Request or Merge Request without explicit user permission.**
- Creating, opening, updating, or driving a PR to clean CI/review does NOT grant permission to merge it.

## Request review and drive every started PR to clean
- Request AI review (`@claude review` / `@agy review`) after completing code pushes.
- Run `ardi` / review loop to drive CI to clean.
- Request human review ONLY after AI approval or deadlock.
